<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item>2.14.1: Modeling Equations to Solve a Riddle</item>
  <item>2.14.2: Finding a Pair of Values that Satisfies Multiple Inequalities</item><list>
    <item>2.14.2: Self Check</item>
    <item>2.14.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  <item>2.14.3: Writing Systems of Inequalities that Represent Situations
    <list>
      <item>2.14.3: Self Check</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>2.14.3: Additional Resources</item>
</list>
  <item>2.14.4: Graphing Solutions of Systems of Inequalities
    <list>
      <item>2.14.4: Self Check</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>2.14.4: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item>2.14.5: Writing Inequalities for Situations and Representing on a Graph</item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 2.14.6: Practice.</para>

<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>Graphing technology</item>
  <item>Optional: notecards</item>
  <item>Graph paper</item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>Acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology. It is ideal if each student has their own device.</para>
<para>Be prepared to display an embedded applet for all to see.</para>

<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para dir="ltr">During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for these words and notice their use and meanings.
  </item>
  <item>
    Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations.
  </item>
  <item>
    Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link>
  </item>
</list> 
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
